(; expect 1 --type-lhs ;)
(; Negative control under --type-lhs: the typing constraint lives under the pattern's binders,
   x, y |- T (t y) == T (b x a), i.e. y == b x a with b definable.  The bound variable y is in
   every reduct of the left side, and no instance of b x a can ever mention it (an instance of the
   pattern variables never does, and reduction adds no free variable): no solution, a fact made by
   firings (the abstracted hypothesis, taken under both binders), whatever rules b gets later. ;)
A : Type.
T : A -> Type.
t : a : A -> T a.
a : A.
def b : A -> A -> A.

def d : X : (A -> A -> A) -> (x : A -> y : A -> T (b x a)) -> Type.
[X] d (x => y => X x y) (x => y => t y) --> A.
